    "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers are mathematically correct and explicitly supported by their own captured worked solutions. No submitted grade or earlier answer is supplied. For q-74629, elimination gives RREF rows (1,0,-21,4), (0,1,6,-1), and (0,0,0,0), so x=21z+4 and y=-6z-1. For q-74626, the RREF rows are (1,0,-10,-1), (0,1,4,1), and zero, giving x=10z-1 and y=1-4z. For q-131647, all equations are multiples of x+2y-4z=3, giving the selected rank-one RREF. For q-74612, the second and third rows are -10 and -4 times the first, leaving the selected first row and two zero rows. Unit tangents are velocity divided by speed: q-127217 has velocity (2,8cos(2t),-8sin(2t)) and speed 2sqrt(17); q-74894 has velocity (2sin(t)+tcos(t),2cos(t)-tsin(t)) and speed sqrt(4+t²); q-33655 has t=1, velocity (4,2,4), and speed 6; q-33584 has t=1, velocity (2,2,1), and speed 3. The product rule gives velocity (1,-1,-1), with speed sqrt(3), for q-75148, and velocity (2,-3,2sqrt(3)), with speed 5, for q-127274. For q-32247, the RREF rows (1,0,10,-8) and (0,1,-6,6) give x₁=-8-10x₃ and x₂=6+6x₃. For q-42019, adding twice the second row to the first gives x=0 and y=z-1. For q-131719, all equations are proportional, leaving one free variable and infinitely many solutions, so II only is true. For q-74634, elimination produces 0=9/2, so III only is true. For q-32246, elimination gives (4-3k)y=0; dependence requires k=4/3. For q-32245, elimination gives (k+2)y=-2; inconsistency requires k=-2. The source has intermediate errors that do not change these final answers: q-74894 writes cross terms with coefficients ±2t instead of ±4t, though they still cancel; q-33584's introductory coordinate formula repeats j where the first basis vector should be i; q-75148 incorrectly labels some normalization steps with t=1 and ‖r(1)‖ instead of t=-1 and ‖r′(-1)‖; q-127274 labels the speed as ‖r(π/4)‖ instead of ‖r′(π/4)‖. Every final answer agrees with the mathematics.",
